What this licence covers, and what it does not:

* It covers the project's own work: the tools, the documentation, the recovered tables in data/, and the source
  code written for this project in src/.
* src/jpeg/ holds the Independent JPEG Group's JPEG library, release 6, unmodified except for the three files
  src/jpeg/README-SDW.md, src/jpeg/jconfig.h and src/jpeg/vc6.json. The IJG files are under the IJG's own terms,
  stated in src/jpeg/README, not under this licence. This software is based in part on the work of the Independent
  JPEG Group.
* Sheep, Dog 'n' Wolf itself - its program, its data and its assets - belongs to its rights holders. The source in
  src/ reproduces the game's program, and it contains the game's own data tables and strings written out as
  initialisers where the original object files defined them. This licence grants no rights to the game; you need
  your own copy of it (and your own copies of the Microsoft tools) to build anything here.
